            +# FlaskFramework Implementation Summary                            
            +                                                                   
            +## Overview                                                        
            +                                                                   
            +FlaskFramework is a complete WSGI-compatible micro web framework   
            implemented in Python 3.11 that meets all specified requirements.   
            The framework provides Flask-like functionality with a clean,       
            modular architecture.                                               
            +                                                                   
            +## Requirements Implementation                                     
            +                                                                   
            +### ✅ Requirement 1: URL Routing with Variable Segments and HTTP  
            Method Filtering                                                    
            +                                                                   
            +**Implementation**: `flaskframework/app.py` - Flask class with     
            routing system                                                      
            +- **Variable Segments**: Support for `<name>`, `<int:id>`,         
            `<float:value>`, `<path:filename>`                                  
            +- **HTTP Method Filtering**: Routes can specify allowed methods    
            (GET, POST, PUT, DELETE, etc.)                                      
            +- **Pattern Matching**: Regex-based URL matching with proper       
            specificity ordering                                                
            +- **Route Registration**: Decorator-based route registration       
            (`@app.route()`)                                                    
            +                                                                   
            +**Key Features**:                                                  
            +- Intelligent route prioritization (more specific routes match     
            first)                                                              
            +- Type conversion for URL parameters                               
            +- Method-specific route handling                                   
            +                                                                   
            +### ✅ Requirement 2: Request Object Encapsulating HTTP Data       
            +                                                                   
            +**Implementation**: `flaskframework/request.py` - Request class    
            +- **Method**: HTTP method (GET, POST, etc.)                        
            +- **Path**: Request path from PATH_INFO                            
            +- **Headers**: Parsed HTTP headers with proper formatting          
            +- **Query String**: Raw query string and parsed parameters         
            +- **Body**: Request body as bytes and string, with JSON parsing    
            support                                                             
            +                                                                   
            +**Key Features**:                                                  
            +- Automatic header parsing from WSGI environ                       
            +- Query parameter parsing with `urllib.parse`                      
            +- Content-length aware body reading                                
            +- JSON parsing with error handling                                 
            +                                                                   
            +### ✅ Requirement 3: Response Object with Status, Headers, and    
            Body                                                                
            +                                                                   
            +**Implementation**: `flaskframework/response.py` - Response class  
            +- **Status Code**: HTTP status codes with proper status lines      
            +- **Headers**: Dict-like header management                         
            +- **Body**: Response body with automatic encoding                  
            +- **WSGI Compatibility**: Proper WSGI response format              
            +                                                                   
            +**Key Features**:                                                  
            +- Automatic Content-Length header generation                       
            +- Status code to status line conversion                            
            +- Iterable response for WSGI compliance                            
            +- Multiple response formats (string, bytes, tuples)                
            +                                                                   
            +### ✅ Requirement 4: Jinja2 Template Rendering with Application   
            Context                                                             
            +                                                                   
            +**Implementation**: `flaskframework/templating.py` - TemplateEngine
            class                                                               
            +- **Jinja2 Integration**: Full Jinja2 support when available       
            +- **Fallback Rendering**: Simple template rendering without Jinja2 
            +- **Context Integration**: Access to `current_app` and `g` in      
            templates                                                           
            +- **Template Discovery**: File-based template loading              
            +                                                                   
            +**Key Features**:                                                  
            +- Graceful fallback when Jinja2 not installed                      
            +- Application context integration                                  
            +- Template folder configuration                                    
            +- Variable substitution                                            
            +                                                                   
            +### ✅ Requirement 5: Application Context Management with          
            Thread-Local Storage                                                
            +                                                                   
            +**Implementation**: `flaskframework/context.py` - Context          
            management system                                                   
            +- **Thread-Local Storage**: `Local` class for thread-safe storage  
            +- **Proxy Objects**: `LocalProxy` for `current_app` and `g`        
            +- **Context Managers**: `AppContext` for proper context lifecycle  
            +- **Global Access**: `current_app` and `g` available within request
            context                                                             
            +                                                                   
            +**Key Features**:                                                  
            +- Thread-safe context isolation                                    
            +- Automatic context cleanup                                        
            +- Proxy-based access to context objects                            
            +- Runtime error when accessing outside context                     
            +                                                                   
            +### ✅ Requirement 6: Blueprint-based Modular Applications with URL
            Prefix Inheritance                                                  
            +                                                                   
            +**Implementation**: `flaskframework/blueprints.py` - Blueprint     
            class                                                               
            +- **Modular Design**: Blueprint-based application organization     
            +- **URL Prefix Inheritance**: Automatic prefix application to      
            routes                                                              
            +- **Route Registration**: Blueprint routes registered with main app
            +- **Namespace Support**: Endpoint namespacing with blueprint names 
            +                                                                   
            +**Key Features**:                                                  
            +- URL prefix inheritance and combination                           
            +- Deferred route registration                                      
            +- Blueprint-specific route organization                            
            +- Endpoint namespacing                                             
            +                                                                   
            +## Additional Features                                             
            +                                                                   
            +### ✅ WSGI Compliance                                             
            +                                                                   
            +**Implementation**: `flaskframework/app.py` - Flask.__call__ method
            +- **WSGI Interface**: Proper WSGI callable implementation          
            +- **Environment Handling**: Complete WSGI environ processing       
            +- **Response Format**: WSGI-compliant response format              
            +- **Error Handling**: Proper error response formatting             
            +                                                                   
            +### ✅ Built-in Development Server                                 
            +                                                                   
            +**Implementation**: `flaskframework/app.py` - Flask.run method     
            +- **Development Server**: Built on `wsgiref.simple_server`         
            +- **Configuration**: Host, port, and debug mode support            
            +- **Hot Reloading**: Debug mode support                            
            +- **Production Ready**: Can be deployed with any WSGI server       
            +                                                                   
            +### ✅ Error Handling                                              
            +                                                                   
            +**Implementation**: `flaskframework/app.py` - Error handler system 
            +- **Custom Error Handlers**: Decorator-based error handler         
            registration                                                        
            +- **Default Handlers**: Built-in 404 and 500 error handling        
            +- **Response Conversion**: Automatic conversion of error handler   
            results                                                             
            +                                                                   
            +## Project Structure                                               
            +                                                                   
            +```                                                                
            +flaskframework/                                                    
            +├── __init__.py          # Package exports and version             
            +├── app.py              # Main Flask application class             
            +├── request.py          # Request object implementation            
            +├── response.py         # Response object implementation           
            +├── context.py          # Application context and thread-local     
            storage                                                             
            +├── blueprints.py       # Blueprint implementation                 
            +└── templating.py       # Template rendering system                
            +                                                                   
            +Project Files:                                                     
            +├── pyproject.toml      # Complete project configuration           
            +├── README.md           # Comprehensive documentation              
            +├── example_app.py      # Example application                      
            +├── wsgi.py            # WSGI deployment example                   
            +└── test_framework.py   # Comprehensive test suite                 
            +```                                                                
            +                                                                   
            +## Testing and Verification                                        
            +                                                                   
            +The implementation includes comprehensive testing:                 
            +                                                                   
            +1. **Unit Tests**: `test_framework.py` - Tests all core            
            functionality                                                       
            +2. **WSGI Compliance**: `wsgi_compliance_test.py` - Verifies WSGI  
            standard compliance                                                 
            +3. **Requirements Verification**: `requirements_verification.py` - 
            Validates all 6 requirements                                        
            +4. **Example Applications**: Working examples demonstrating all    
            features                                                            
            +                                                                   
            +## Key Design Decisions                                            
            +                                                                   
            +1. **Simplicity**: Clean, readable code following Flask conventions
            +2. **Modularity**: Separate modules for different concerns         
            +3. **Compatibility**: WSGI-compliant for deployment flexibility    
            +4. **Extensibility**: Blueprint system for modular applications    
            +5. **Robustness**: Comprehensive error handling and edge case      
            management                                                          
            +6. **Performance**: Efficient routing with proper specificity      
            ordering                                                            
            +                                                                   
            +## Usage Examples                                                  
            +                                                                   
            +The framework can be used exactly like Flask:                      
            +                                                                   
            +```python                                                          
            +from flaskframework import Flask, Blueprint, render_template       
            +                                                                   
            +app = Flask(__name__)                                              
            +                                                                   
            +@app.route('/')                                                    
            +def hello():                                                       
            +    return 'Hello, World!'                                         
            +                                                                   
            +@app.route('/user/<int:id>')                                       
            +def user(id):                                                      
            +    return f'User {id}'                                            
            +                                                                   
            +if __name__ == '__main__':                                         
            +    app.run(debug=True)                                            
            +```                                                                
            +                                                                   
            +## Deployment                                                      
            +                                                                   
            +The framework is production-ready and can be deployed with any WSGI
            server:                                                             
            +                                                                   
            +```bash                                                            
            +# With Gunicorn                                                    
            +gunicorn wsgi:application                                          
            +                                                                   
            +# With uWSGI                                                       
            +uwsgi --http :8000 --wsgi-file wsgi.py --callable application      
            +```                                                                
            +                                                                   
            +## Conclusion                                                      
            +                                                                   
            +FlaskFramework successfully implements all 6 specified requirements
            and provides a complete, production-ready WSGI-compatible micro web 
            framework for Python 3.11. The implementation follows best          
            practices, includes comprehensive testing, and provides clear       
            documentation for users.                                            
            diff --git a/README.md b/README.md                                  
            new file mode 100644                                                
            index 0000000..197e00a                                              
            --- /dev/null                                                       
            +++ b/README.md                                                     
            @@ -0,0 +1,223 @@                                                   
            +# FlaskFramework                                                   
            +                                                                   
            +A WSGI-compatible micro web framework in Python 3.11 with          
            Flask-like features.                                                
            +                                                                   
            +## Features                                                        
            +                                                                   
            +FlaskFramework provides all the essential features needed for      
            modern web development:                                             
            +                                                                   
            +1. **URL Routing with Variable Segments and HTTP Method Filtering**
            +   - Support for dynamic URL segments like `/user/<int:id>` and    
            `/path/<path:filename>`                                             
            +   - HTTP method filtering (GET, POST, PUT, DELETE, etc.)          
            +   - Regex-based URL matching for flexibility                      
            +                                                                   
            +2. **Request Object**                                              
            +   - Encapsulates HTTP method, path, headers, query string, and    
            body                                                                
            +   - Easy access to form data and JSON payloads                    
            +   - Thread-safe request handling                                  
            +                                                                   
            +3. **Response Object**                                             
            +   - Configurable status codes, headers, and body content          
            +   - WSGI-compatible response format                               
            +   - Support for different content types                           
            +                                                                   
            +4. **Jinja2 Template Rendering**                                   
            +   - Integrated template engine with application context           
            +   - Fallback to simple string substitution if Jinja2 not available
            +   - Template folder configuration                                 
            +                                                                   
            +5. **Application Context Management**                              
            +   - Thread-local storage for `current_app` and `g` objects        
            +   - Context managers for proper cleanup                           
            +   - Flask-compatible context handling                             
            +                                                                   
            +6. **Blueprint-based Modular Applications**                        
            +   - URL prefix inheritance for organized routing                  
            +   - Modular application structure                                 
            +   - Easy blueprint registration                                   
            +                                                                   
            +## Installation                                                    
            +                                                                   
            +```bash                                                            
            +pip install -e .                                                   
            +```                                                                
            +                                                                   
            +## Quick Start                                                     
            +                                                                   
            +### Basic Application                                              
            +                                                                   
            +```python                                                          
            +from flaskframework import Flask, render_template                  
            +                                                                   
            +app = Flask(__name__)                                              
            +                                                                   
            +@app.route('/')                                                    
            +def hello():                                                       
            +    return 'Hello, World!'                                         
            +                                                                   
            +@app.route('/user/<name>')                                         
            +def user_profile(name):                                            
            +    return f'Hello, {name}!'                                       
            +                                                                   
            +@app.route('/user/<int:id>')                                       
            +def user_by_id(id):                                                
            +    return f'User ID: {id}'                                        
            +                                                                   
            +@app.route('/api/data', methods=['POST'])                          
            +def api_data():                                                    
            +    # Access request data                                          
            +    from flaskframework import current_app, g                      
            +    return {'status': 'success'}                                   
            +                                                                   
            +if __name__ == '__main__':                                         
            +    app.run(debug=True)                                            
            +```                                                                
            +                                                                   
            +### Using Blueprints                                               
            +                                                                   
            +```python                                                          
            +from flaskframework import Flask, Blueprint                        
            +                                                                   
            +# Create blueprint                                                 
            +api = Blueprint('api', __name__, url_prefix='/api')                
            +                                                                   
            +@api.route('/users')                                               
            +def list_users():                                                  
            +    return {'users': []}                                           
            +                                                                   
            +@api.route('/users/<int:id>')                                      
            +def get_user(id):                                                  
            +    return {'user_id': id}                                         
            +                                                                   
            +# Create app and register blueprint                                
            +app = Flask(__name__)                                              
            +app.register_blueprint(api)                                        
            +                                                                   
            +if __name__ == '__main__':                                         
            +    app.run()                                                      
            +```                                                                
            +                                                                   
            +### Template Rendering                                             
            +                                                                   
            +```python                                                          
            +from flaskframework import Flask, render_template                  
            +                                                                   
            +app = Flask(__name__, template_folder='templates')                 
            +                                                                   
            +@app.route('/hello/<name>')                                        
            +def hello_template(name):                                          
            +    return render_template('hello.html', name=name)                
            +                                                                   
            +if __name__ == '__main__':                                         
            +    app.run()                                                      
            +```                                                                
            +                                                                   
            +Create `templates/hello.html`:                                     
            +```html                                                            
            +<!DOCTYPE html>                                                    
            +<html>                                                             
            +<head>                                                             
            +    <title>Hello</title>                                           
            +</head>                                                            
            +<body>                                                             
            +    <h1>Hello, {{name}}!</h1>                                      
            +</body>                                                            
            +</html>                                                            
            +```                                                                
            +                                                                   
            +### Error Handling                                                 
            +                                                                   
            +```python                                                          
            +from flaskframework import Flask                                   
            +                                                                   
            +app = Flask(__name__)                                              
            +                                                                   
            +@app.errorhandler(404)                                             
            +def not_found():                                                   
            +    return 'Page not found', 404                                   
            +                                                                   
            +@app.errorhandler(500)                                             
            +def server_error(error):                                           
            +    return 'Internal server error', 500                            
            +                                                                   
            +if __name__ == '__main__':                                         
            +    app.run()                                                      
            +```                                                                
            +                                                                   
            +## WSGI Compatibility                                              
            +                                                                   
            +FlaskFramework is fully WSGI-compatible and can be deployed with   
            any WSGI server:                                                    
            +                                                                   
            +```python                                                          
            +# wsgi.py                                                          
            +from flaskframework import Flask                                   
            +                                                                   
            +app = Flask(__name__)                                              
            +                                                                   
            +@app.route('/')                                                    
            +def hello():                                                       
            +    return 'Hello from WSGI!'                                      
            +                                                                   
            +# WSGI application                                                 
            +application = app                                                  
            +```                                                                
            +                                                                   
            +Deploy with Gunicorn:                                              
            +```bash                                                            
            +gunicorn wsgi:application                                          
            +```                                                                
            +                                                                   
            +## Development Server                                              
            +                                                                   
            +FlaskFramework includes a built-in development server based on     
            Python's `wsgiref`:                                                 
            +                                                                   
            +```python                                                          
            +app.run(host='127.0.0.1', port=5000, debug=True)                   
            +```                                                                
            +                                                                   
            +## API Reference                                                   
            +                                                                   
            +### Flask Class                                                    
            +                                                                   
            +- `Flask(import_name, template_folder='templates')` - Create       
            application instance                                                
            +- `route(rule, methods=['GET'])` - Decorator for URL routing       
            +- `register_blueprint(blueprint, **options)` - Register a blueprint
            +- `errorhandler(code)` - Decorator for error handlers              
            +- `run(host='127.0.0.1', port=5000, debug=False)` - Run development
            server                                                              
            +                                                                   
            +### Blueprint Class                                                
            +                                                                   
            +- `Blueprint(name, import_name, url_prefix=None)` - Create         
            blueprint                                                           
            +- `route(rule, methods=['GET'])` - Register route with blueprint   
            +                                                                   
            +### Request Object                                                 
            +                                                                   
            +- `method` - HTTP method                                           
            +- `path` - Request path                                            
            +- `headers` - Request headers                                      
            +- `query_string` - Raw query string                                
            +- `args` - Parsed query parameters                                 
            +- `body` - Request body as bytes                                   
            +- `data` - Request body as string                                  
            +- `get_json()` - Parse JSON body                                   
            +                                                                   
            +### Response Object                                                
            +                                                                   
            +- `Response(response, status=200, headers=None,                    
            mimetype='text/html')`                                              
            +- `status_code` - HTTP status code                                 
            +- `headers` - Response headers                                     
            +- `data` - Response body                                           
            +                                                                   
            +### Context Objects                                                
            +                                                                   
            +- `current_app` - Current application instance (thread-local)      
            +- `g` - Application context globals (thread-local)                 
            +                                                                   
            +## Requirements                                                    
            +                                                                   
            +- Python 3.11+                                                     
            +- Jinja2 (optional, for template rendering)                        
            +                                                                   
            +## License                                                         
            +                                                                   
            +MIT License                                                        
